{
  "__comment": "A platform team's interface to a running sidecar is a dashboard, not a scrape endpoint (U2, G239). Import this into Grafana and pick the Prometheus that scrapes kube-noob's /metrics; every query below names only a metric src/kube_noob/server/metrics.py actually emits, and a test asserts that, because a panel referencing a metric that does not exist is the same class of claim as a document quoting a count that stopped being true. Counters are per process and the chart runs one pod, so these are that pod's numbers.",
  "title": "kube-noob",
  "uid": "kube-noob",
  "tags": ["kube-noob", "mcp"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {"from": "now-6h", "to": "now"},
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "job",
        "label": "Job",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
        "query": "label_values(kube_noob_build_info, job)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it up, and what is it",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Version",
      "description": "From kube_noob_build_info. The label, not a guess: this is the build that is answering.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 5, "x": 0, "y": 1},
      "options": {"textMode": "name", "colorMode": "none", "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "kube_noob_build_info{job=\"$job\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{version}} ({{platform}})",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Uptime",
      "description": "Seconds since this process started serving. A reset means the pod restarted, which also resets every counter on this dashboard.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 5, "x": 5, "y": 1},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "s"}, "overrides": []},
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}},
      "targets": [{"refId": "A", "expr": "kube_noob_uptime_seconds{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "uptime"}]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Age of the built-in knowledge",
      "description": "kube_noob_knowledge_age_seconds. This is the age of the knowledge in the IMAGE, fixed when it was built -- not a failed refresh. Answers about releases newer than that come only from web lookups you enable. Update the image, or ignore this if the version is pinned deliberately.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 7, "x": 10, "y": 1},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "yellow", "value": 3888000},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 7776000}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}},
      "targets": [{"refId": "A", "expr": "kube_noob_knowledge_age_seconds{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "age"}]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Calls in the window",
      "description": "Every tool call this process served, by outcome. A pod restart resets it.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 4, "w": 7, "x": 17, "y": 1},
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]}},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(kube_noob_tool_calls_total{job=\"$job\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "What is being asked, and how it is going",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 5},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Calls per second, by outcome",
      "description": "invalid-arguments is a caller sending bad input, which is not this pod failing: it is shown separately for that reason, and the KubeNoobToolErrorRatio alert excludes it.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 6},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "reqps", "custom": {"fillOpacity": 20, "stacking": {"mode": "normal"}}}, "overrides": []},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(kube_noob_tool_calls_total{job=\"$job\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failure ratio",
      "description": "crash + error over all calls, the same expression the KubeNoobToolErrorRatio alert uses, so what pages you is what you see here.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 6},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "percentunit", "min": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(kube_noob_tool_calls_total{job=\"$job\",outcome=~\"crash|error\"}[15m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(kube_noob_tool_calls_total{job=\"$job\"}[15m])), 1e-9)",
          "legendFormat": "crash + error"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "barchart",
      "title": "Which tools are used",
      "description": "By tool over the dashboard's window. Tool names come from a fixed set; an unexpected one is reported as `other` rather than growing the label space.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 14},
      "options": {"orientation": "horizontal", "xTickLabelRotation": 0},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "topk(15, sum by (tool) (increase(kube_noob_tool_calls_total{job=\"$job\"}[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool}}",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration, 50th and 95th percentile",
      "description": "From kube_noob_tool_duration_seconds. Histogram buckets are coarse on purpose (10 of them), so read these as the shape of the latency rather than an exact figure.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 14},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "s", "min": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(kube_noob_tool_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(kube_noob_tool_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Slowest tools, 95th percentile",
      "description": "Which tool is costing the time. A corpus search is hundreds of milliseconds by nature; an audit that moves into seconds is worth looking at.",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 23},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "s", "min": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "topk(8, histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (tool, le) (rate(kube_noob_tool_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[10m]))))",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
